# Bilingual German Readers — this repo commits ONLY the reusable procedure,
# scripts, and documentation. The actual book content is intentionally NOT
# committed: downloaded Project Gutenberg texts, the per-book translations
# (markdown), and the generated PDFs/EPUBs are large and for personal study
# only — they are regenerated on demand from the procedure.
#
# Strategy: ignore everything at the repo root, then allow-list the tooling.
# This way any NEW book folder you download later is ignored automatically.

/*

# --- keep (the procedure + scripts + docs) ---
!/.gitignore
!/README.md
!/CLAUDE.md
!/instruction.md
!/prompt.md
!/sample.png
!/build/
!/docs/

# --- never track these anywhere, even inside allowed dirs ---
*.pdf
*.epub
.DS_Store
.claude/

# --- except published downloads: public-domain books, safe to distribute ---
!/releases/
!/releases/*.epub
!/releases/*.pdf

# Notes:
# - texts/   — local cache of downloaded Project Gutenberg .txt files (one folder
#              per book). Ignored. Not needed in the repo: re-downloadable from
#              gutenberg.org on demand; kept only to avoid re-downloading.
# - books/   — the working directory: per-book dirs with source/, markdown/,
#              markdown/parts/, build/, pdf/, grammar-test/. Ignored (large;
#              personal study; regenerated on demand).
# - The canonical, generic build assets live in /build and ARE committed; the
#   procedure copies them into each book's  books/<book>/build/.
